15. IPV6 DNS TROUBLESHOOTING

One of the problems during the domain setup was that the client was using IPv6 DNS.

This caused problems with domain discovery and joining the Active Directory domain.

I opened:

Control Panel
→ Network and Internet
→ Network and Sharing Center
→ Change adapter settings

I opened the Ethernet adapter properties.

I disabled:

Internet Protocol Version 6 (TCP/IPv6)

I then checked the IPv4 settings.

The preferred DNS server was:

192.168.64.2

After making the change, I tested:

nltest /dsgetdc:matthias.local

The client successfully found:

DC01.matthias.local

This fixed the domain discovery issue.

