35. MY GENERAL HELP DESK TROUBLESHOOTING PROCESS

When troubleshooting an Active Directory issue, my process is:

1. Identify the user's problem.
2. Ask what changed.
3. Reproduce the problem if possible.
4. Check the user's account.
5. Check whether the account is enabled.
6. Check whether the account is locked.
7. Check the password.
8. Check password expiration.
9. Check group membership.
10. Check OU placement.
11. Check Group Policy.
12. Check the client's IP address.
13. Check DNS.
14. Ping the Domain Controller.
15. Test domain discovery.
16. Check Event Viewer.
17. Make the appropriate change.
18. Test the solution.
19. Confirm the issue is resolved.
20. Document the ticket.
21. Escalate if necessary.

